id: pm-alhqbz
title: "GH-933: nested PM writes in non-PM linked tests can mutate the source project"
description: "A linked test whose outer command is not pm still exports PM_SOURCE_PM_PATH and PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT. A nested package lifecycle can therefore run a mutating pm command such as merge install against the source workspace. Preserve cross-project validation from GH-689 while making nested source-context mutation an explicit opt-in or a fail-closed boundary. GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/933"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: context-integrity,linked-tests,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-08-08T10:14:38.912Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T10:34:24.008Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-08T10:32:57.708Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-08T10:32:57.708Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Non-PM linked tests cannot silently mutate the source PM workspace through nested pm lifecycle commands; validation/read workflows retain the source identity they need; explicit opt-in is typed, documented, and observable; unit, integration, negative-control, full coverage, and temporary installed-package acceptance pass"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Nested package lifecycles retain source identity for validation but cannot mutate source merge configuration implicitly; one explicit typed override is available and observable.
actual_result: "Linked-test source context is now read-only by contract. Nested merge-install writes select the sibling workspace, dry-run source reads remain compatible, protected environment keys prevent metadata bypass, and an explicit override is exposed through the public SDK resolver."
fixed_version: 2026.8.8
